      "id": "sol.amc-8-2003-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Art’s cookie area is \\(12\\) square inches, so the whole batch has area \\(12\\cdot12=144\\) square inches.\n\nTrisha’s triangular cookie has area \\(\\frac12\\cdot3\\cdot4=6\\) square inches.\n\nTherefore Trisha can make \\(144\\div6=24\\) cookies per batch.\n\nThus, E is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Trisha’s cookie area is half of Art’s cookie area.",
        "Same dough amount means half-size cookies make twice as many."
      ],
